# draft
// FIRST DRAFT (game phase 8, docs/tech-spec.md §74): rewrite or sign off. Voice: docs/voice.md. Flags: docs/story-drafts.md.
// Night 6, after the night's own scene, while your mother is at home: her friend Oddny, and a favour.
EXTERNAL flag(name)
# fx: flag errand_oddny
A late raven brings a letter from your mother, folded small, as if she didn't want it seen.
"Oddny Grimsdottir died this week. The coughing sickness. We grew up on farms that shared a wall, and a goat, and most of our secrets." # speaker: mother
"When we were girls she used to say she'd dance in Freyja's meadow when she died. She said it so often it stopped being a joke." # speaker: mother
"If she comes to your gate, could you send her there? Just her. I've never asked you for anything, and I know it isn't your rule." # speaker: mother
* [Promise to look for her.]
  # fx: flag oddny_promised
  You write that you'll look for her. You don't write what you'll do when you find her.
* [Tell her you can only judge by the rules.]
  You write that the rules are the rules, and that you're sorry. It reads worse than you meant it to.
- The raven takes it, and doesn't look at you.
-> END
